  "solution": {
    "text": "Cellulose is a straight chain polysaccharide composed of D-glucose units, which are joined by $\\beta$-glycosidic linkages between $\\mathrm{C}-1$ of one glucose and C-4 of the next glucose. In one, unit only three hydroxy groups are free to form acetate, that's why called cellulose triacetate",
